<title>INDIA: India cuts capital gains tax for expatriates.</title>
<headline>India cuts capital gains tax for expatriates.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian Finance Minister P. Chidambaram on Friday proposed cutting the capital gains tax on securities for non-resident Indians (NRIs) to 10 percent from 20 percent.</p>
<p>Chidambaram, presenting the budget for 1997/98 (April-March), said the proposal conferred the same status on expatriate investors as on foreign institutional investors (FIIs).</p>
